<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <%
        const aboutExportValues = (Array.isArray(exportFormats) ? exportFormats : [])
            .map((format) => String(format?.value || '').trim().toLowerCase())
            .filter(Boolean);
        const aboutLegacyExportsEnabled = aboutExportValues.some((value) => value !== 'ltd');
        const aboutQrExportsEnabled = aboutExportValues.includes('qr');
        const pageTitle = 'About InfiniMii - Mii Archive and Tools';
        const pageDesc = aboutLegacyExportsEnabled
            ? 'InfiniMii is a Mii archive with sharing, rendering, file conversion, and transfer guides.'
            : 'InfiniMii is a Mii archive with sharing, LTD previews, file conversion, and transfer guides.';
        const canonicalUrl = `${baseUrl}/about`;
        const keywords = 'about infinimii, mii platform, mii repository, mii community';
        const breadcrumbs = [
            { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
            { name: 'About', url: '/about' }
        ];
        const schemaType = 'AboutPage';
        %>
        <%- include('metaTags', { title: pageTitle, description: pageDesc, canonicalUrl, keywords }) %>
        <%- include('structuredData') %>
        
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/global.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/utilityPages.css">
        <style>
            li{
                list-style-type:disc;
                margin:0px;
            }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <%- include('globalStyle') %>
        <%- include('header') %>
        <%- include('accountDisplay') %>
        
        <main class="content about-content" role="main">
            <%- include('sidebar') %>
            
            <article class="about-article guide-container">
                
                <article class="intro-article">
                    <h1>About InfiniMii</h1>
                    <p class="lead"><%= aboutLegacyExportsEnabled
                        ? 'InfiniMii archives Mii characters and provides tools for sharing, rendering, file conversion, and transfers between Nintendo systems.'
                        : 'InfiniMii archives Mii characters and provides tools for sharing, rendering, and transfers. Original LTD files remain unchanged, while Miis from other systems can use compatible conversion options.' %></p>
                </article>
                
                <article class="features-article">
                    <h2>What InfiniMii does</h2>
                    
                    <div class="feature-grid">
                        <div class="feature-card">
                            <h3><%- include('icon', { name: 'gamepad', size: 20, class: 'icon-inline icon-primary' }) %> Supported systems</h3>
                            <p>InfiniMii works with Miis from these Nintendo systems and services:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Nintendo DS</li>
                                <li>Nintendo Wii</li>
                                <li>Nintendo 3DS</li>
                                <li>Nintendo Wii U</li>
                                <li>Amiibo</li>
                                <li>Nintendo Switch</li>
                                <li>Switch 2</li>
                                <li>Mii Studio</li>
                                <li>Tomodachi Life</li>
                                <li>Miitomo</li>
                            </ul>
                            <a href="/transferInstructions">Read the transfer guide</a>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="feature-card">
                            <h3><%- include('icon', { name: 'refresh', size: 20, class: 'icon-inline icon-primary' }) %> File conversion</h3>
                            <p><%= aboutLegacyExportsEnabled ? 'Available conversion tools include:' : 'Supported Mii files can be converted to LTD from:' %></p>
                            <% if (aboutLegacyExportsEnabled) { %>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Wii ↔ 3DS/Wii U backporting</li>
                                <li>QR code generation</li>
                                <li>Binary file conversion</li>
                                <li>Special format variants</li>
                                <li>Extract Miis from and insert Miis into Amiibo files</li>
                                <li>Lossless conversion where possible</li>
                            </ul>
                            <% } else { %>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Wii, 3DS, Wii U, Switch, and related source formats</li>
                                    <li>Binary Mii file conversion</li>
                                    <li>Extract Miis from Amiibo files</li>
                                    <li>Appearance data retained when the source format allows it</li>
                                </ul>
                            <% } %>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="feature-card">
                            <h3><%- include('icon', { name: 'book-open', size: 20, class: 'icon-inline icon-primary' }) %> Mii archive</h3>
                            <p>Browse:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Official Nintendo Miis from games</li>
                                <li>Community-created characters</li>
                                <li>Celebrity and character recreations</li>
                                <li>Original designs</li>
                                <li>The statistically Average Mii</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="feature-card">
                            <h3><%- include('icon', { name: 'qr-code', size: 20, class: 'icon-inline icon-primary' }) %> QR code <%= aboutQrExportsEnabled ? 'tools' : 'input' %></h3>
                            <p><%= aboutQrExportsEnabled ? 'Read and create compatible Mii QR codes:' : 'Start with a compatible Mii QR code:' %></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Scan QR codes from images</li>
                                <% if (aboutQrExportsEnabled) { %>
                                    <li>Generate compatible QR codes</li>
                                    <li>3DS/Wii U workflows</li>
                                <% } else { %>
                                    <li>Convert decoded Miis to LTD</li>
                                    <li>Upload decoded Miis to InfiniMii</li>
                                <% } %>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="feature-card">
                            <h3><%- include('icon', { name: 'lock', size: 20, class: 'icon-inline icon-primary' }) %> Private Mii collection</h3>
                            <p>Keep Miis private until you choose to publish them:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Store Miis privately online</li>
                                <li>Access from any device</li>
                                <li>Sync between systems</li>
                                <li>Family and friend Miis</li>
                                <li>Backup your creations</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </article>
                
                <article class="average-mii-article">
                    <h2>The Average Mii</h2>
                    <p><strong>The Average Mii</strong> uses the most common feature choices and placements among Miis in the database. It is recalculated as the collection changes.</p>
                    <a href="/mii/average" class="btn-primary">View the Average Mii</a>
                </article>
                
                <!--article class="community-article">
                    <h2>Join the Community</h2>
                    <p>InfiniMii is built by people who make, share, and document Miis.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Monthly Contests</strong> - Create Miis based on themes, with top submissions featured</li>
                        <li><strong>Official Mii Research</strong> - Apply here to help document official Miis</li>
                        <li><strong>Further Development</strong> - We're open source! Contribute to improving InfiniMii and the MiiJS library that powers it!</li>
                        <li><strong>Community Sharing</strong> - Share your best creations with fellow enthusiasts</li>
                    </ul>
                    <a href="<%= discordInvite %>" class="btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join Our Discord</a>
                </article-->
                
                <article class="technology-article">
                    <h2>Built with MiiJS</h2>
                    <p>InfiniMii uses <strong>MiiJS</strong>, an open-source JavaScript library for reading and writing Mii data, alongside a renderer based on recovered LTD source code. They support:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Reading and writing supported Mii formats, including LTD</li>
                        <li>Transparent LTD previews for compatible Miis; files that use unverified data receive no generated preview</li>
                        <li>Reading and creating QR codes</li>
                        <li>Format conversion while retaining supported data</li>
                        <li>Creating recreation instructions</li>
                        <li>Using the same Mii tools in other projects</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>MiiJS is available on GitHub and NPM for developers who want to build their own Mii applications.</p>
                    <a href="https://github.com/Stewared/MiiJS" class="btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View MiiJS on GitHub</a>
                </article>

                <article class="open-source-article">
                    <h2>Open Source</h2>
                    <p>InfiniMii and MiiJS are free and open source. Their code is available to inspect and contribute to. InfiniMii has no ads or paid feature tiers.</p>
                </article>
                
                <article class="disclaimer-article">
                    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
                    <p>InfiniMii is an independent fan project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or associated with Nintendo Co., Ltd. Nintendo, Mii, Wii, Nintendo DS, Nintendo 3DS, Wii U, Amiibo, Nintendo Switch, Switch 2, Tomodachi Life, and Miitomo are trademarks of Nintendo Co., Ltd.</p>
                </article>
            </article>
            
            <%- include('featuredMiis') %>
        </main>
        
        <%- include('footer') %>
    </body>
</html>
